# WLISTTM.KEY - the seeks of the list window: letters (wl_letters),
# wl_find and a lead row (wl_lead); TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WLISTTM.SNP.
# The IDs are left-aligned, so a row's text starts with its key.
S START
# Without letters a character typed does nothing.
T 3
S NOLETTER
# With letters, 3 seeks item 3, on the second page: a busy move; 1
# goes on past the last row to the first.
K SHIFT-F4
S LETTERS
T 3
S THREE
T 1
S ONE
# A character no row starts with walks round to the row it started on.
T X
S NONE
# F4 fetches the list again from its first page and seeks item 3, from
# item 1 again when it was there already.
K F4
S FOUND
K F4
S AGAIN
# SHIFT-F7 posts an Esc, then finds item 1, the first row, at once: one
# request for the first page, no walk to fetch the second or wait and
# take the Esc, which is still queued (FIRST 1 1).
K SHIFT-F7
S FIRST
# CTRL-F4: the list made again with a lead row, key 0, before the
# items; Enter on it opens 0.  Letters are off in the new list.
K CTRL-F4
S LEAD
K ENTER
S OPENLEAD
T 2
S LEADCHAR
K DOWN DOWN
S LEADDOWN
K ESC
